jmt8@po.CWRU.Edu (James M. Trela) writes:
>first of all, you need a wand of polymorph.
>next stack a whole bunch of "useless" items on a square.
>zap the wand at the square.

Uh, it's best to find out the blessed/cursed status and the enchantment of
armour first.  To do this, find an altar and drop all stuff on it.  Junk all
cursed items.  Wear the armour to find out the enchantment.  Now make two 
piles:  One with uncursed +0 armour and uncursed tools, the other one with 
blessed and/or +X armour and blessed tools.  Start polypiling.  Polymorphing 
does not affect the enchantment and blessed status of things, so the things 
in the "good" pile will always stay enchanted/blessed, while the things in
the other pile will always be +0 and uncursed.

>you'll get different items than you started with.
>ie.  all weapons will still be weapons buy a different kind.
>	potions will change to different potions, etc.
>i believe that all food or corpses turn into food rations.

Yes, and dragon corpses will turn into dragon scale mail.  But don't poly-
morph dragon scale mail again, it will turn into "normal" armour.

